ere's a summary of what the regex does:\n\n## Regex Components:\n\n1. **Line requirement**: `^(?=.*IPv4_PATTERN)` - ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address\n2. **IPv4 pattern**: `(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d\\d|[1-9]?\\d)\\.(...repeated 3 times...)` - matches 0-255 per octet without leading zeros\n3. **Date pattern**: \n   - 31-day months (Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Aug, Oct, Dec): days 01-31\n   - 30-day months (Apr, Jun, Sep, Nov): days 01-30\n   - February: days 01-29 (as required)\n4. **Last date selection**: `(?!.*DATE_PATTERN)` - negative lookahead ensures no more dates follow\n5. **Word boundaries**: `(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])` and `(?![a-zA-Z0-9])` - prevents false matches like \"1134-12-1234\"\n\n## Validation Results:\n- ✓ Matches only the last date when multiple dates exist\n- ✓ Rejects lines without IPv4 addresses\n- ✓ Validates month-specific day limits\n- ✓ Allows February up to 29 days\n- ✓ Rejects IPv4 octets with leading zeros (like 01.002.003.004)\n- ✓ Rejects IPv4 octets > 255\n- ✓ Enforces word boundaries to avoid false matches\n\nThe regex is ready at `/app/regex.txt` for use with `re.findall()`.","ttft_ms":149184,"type":"result","duration_ms":234333,"uuid":"28ea5ec3-491d-4043-bd63-11130fa35b3d","ttft_stream_ms":18513,"time_to_request_ms":78,"queued_turn_count":0}
